      "writtenOn": "2026-07-10T17:59:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I read that and dug even deeper to find that is_rtl effectively controls whether or not we call pdfium::unicode::GetMirrorChar() and also if it\u0027s true it forces unicode normalization.\n\nSince GetMirrorChar() has absolutely no documentation (nor does the is_rtl parameter) I had to ask gemini and it told me that GetMirrorChar() converts ( to ) and ] to [ etc. So I think it\u0027s correct that we don\u0027t want this on for /ActualText.\n\nIt would be more helpful if we had comments either here or in the docs for AddCharInfo to explain what\u0027s happening and why.",
      "parentUuid": "e23848fd_1d781f5f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 858,
        "startChar": 31,
        "endLine": 858,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "515aae3212b079283c30176d5ec7348ce9de79fb",
      "serverId": "fca2d64a-0420-3532-b200-12848c95a47b"
    },
